[{"answer":"Producing enough energy to meet our needs has become a serious problem.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/1-2024-11-05-15-43-04.mp3"},{"answer":"Demand is rising rapidly,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/2.mp3"},{"answer":"because of the world's increasing population and expanding industry.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/3.mp3"},{"answer":"Burning fossil fuels, like gas, coal and oil,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/4.mp3"},{"answer":"seriously damages the environment","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/5.mp3"},{"answer":"and they'll eventually run out.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/6.mp3"},{"answer":"For a number of years now,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/7.mp3"},{"answer":"scientists have been working out how we can derive energy from renewable sources,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/8.mp3"},{"answer":"such as the sun and wind, without causing pollution.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/9.mp3"},{"answer":"Today I'll outline marine renewable energy - also called ocean energy -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/10.mp3"},{"answer":"which harnesses the movement of the oceans.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/11.mp3"},{"answer":"Marine renewable energy can be divided into three main categories:","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/12.mp3"},{"answer":"wave energy, tidal energy and ocean thermal energy conversion,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/13.mp3"},{"answer":"and I'll say a few words about each one.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/14.mp3"},{"answer":"First, wave energy.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/15.mp3"},{"answer":"Numerous devices have been invented to harvest wave energy,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/16.mp3"},{"answer":"with names such as Wave Dragon, the Penguin and Mighty Whale,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/17.mp3"},{"answer":"and research is going on to try and come up with a really efficient method.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/18.mp3"},{"answer":"This form of energy has plenty of potential, as the source is constant,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/19.mp3"},{"answer":"and there's no danger of waves coming to a standstill.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/20.mp3"},{"answer":"Electricity can be generated using onshore systems,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/21.mp3"},{"answer":"using a reservoir, or offshore systems.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/22.mp3"},{"answer":"But the problem with ocean waves is that they're erratic,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/23.mp3"},{"answer":"with the winds making them travel in every direction.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/24.mp3"},{"answer":"This adds to the difficulty of creating efficient technology:","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/25.mp3"},{"answer":"ideally all the waves would travel smoothly and regularly along the same straight line.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/26.mp3"},{"answer":"Another drawback is that sand and other sediment on the ocean floor","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/27.mp3"},{"answer":"might be stopped from flowing normally,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/28.mp3"},{"answer":"which can lead to environmental problems.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/29.mp3"},{"answer":"The second category of marine energy that I'll mention is tidal energy.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/30.mp3"},{"answer":"One major advantage of using the tide, rather than waves, as a source of energy","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/31.mp3"},{"answer":"is that it's predictable:","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/32.mp3"},{"answer":"we know the exact times of high and low tides for years to come.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/33.mp3"},{"answer":"For tidal energy to be effective,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/34.mp3"},{"answer":"the difference between high and low tides needs to be at least five metres,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/35.mp3"},{"answer":"and this occurs naturally in only about forty places on Earth.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/36.mp3"},{"answer":"But the right conditions can be created by constructing a tidal lagoon,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/37.mp3"},{"answer":"an area of sea water separated from the sea.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/38.mp3"},{"answer":"One current plan is to create a tidal lagoon on the coast of Wales.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/39.mp3"},{"answer":"This will be an area of water within a bay at Swansea,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/40.mp3"},{"answer":"sheltered by a U-shaped breakwater, or dam, built out from the coast.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/41.mp3"},{"answer":"The breakwater will contain sixteen hydro turbines,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/42.mp3"},{"answer":"and as the tide rises, water rushes through the breakwater,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/43.mp3"},{"answer":"activating the turbines, which turn a generator to produce electricity.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/44.mp3"},{"answer":"Then, for three hours as the tide goes out,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/45.mp3"},{"answer":"the water is held back within the breakwater,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/46.mp3"},{"answer":"increasing the difference in water level,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/47.mp3"},{"answer":"until it's several metres higher within the lagoon than in the open sea.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/48.mp3"},{"answer":"Then, in order to release the stored water,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/49.mp3"},{"answer":"gates in the breakwater are opened.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/50.mp3"},{"answer":"It pours powerfully out of the lagoon,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/51.mp3"},{"answer":"driving the turbines in the breakwater in the opposite direction","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/52.mp3"},{"answer":"and again generating thousands of megawatts of electricity.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/53.mp3"},{"answer":"As there are two high tides a day,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/54.mp3"},{"answer":"this lagoon scheme would generate electricity four times a day, every day,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/55.mp3"},{"answer":"for a total of around 14 hours in every 24,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/56.mp3"},{"answer":"and enough electricity for over 150,000 homes.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/57.mp3"},{"answer":"This system has quite a lot in its favour:","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/58.mp3"},{"answer":"unlike solar and wind energy it doesn't depend on the weather;","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/59.mp3"},{"answer":"the turbines are operated without the need for fuel,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/60.mp3"},{"answer":"so it doesn't create any greenhouse gas emissions;","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/61.mp3"},{"answer":"and very little maintenance is needed.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/62.mp3"},{"answer":"It's estimated that electricity generated in this way will be relatively cheap,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/63.mp3"},{"answer":"and that manufacturing the components would create more than 2,000 jobs,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/64.mp3"},{"answer":"a big boost to the local economy.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/65.mp3"},{"answer":"On the other hand,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/66.mp3"},{"answer":"there are fears that lagoons might harm both fish and birds,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/67.mp3"},{"answer":"for example by disturbing migration patterns,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/68.mp3"},{"answer":"and causing a build-up of silt, affecting local ecosystems.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/69.mp3"},{"answer":"There are other forms of tidal energy,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/70.mp3"},{"answer":"but I'll go on to the third category of marine energy:","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/71.mp3"},{"answer":"ocean thermal energy conversion.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/72.mp3"},{"answer":"This depends on there being a big difference in temperature","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/73.mp3"},{"answer":"between surface water and the water a couple of kilometres below the surface,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/74.mp3"},{"answer":"and this occurs in tropical coastal areas.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/75.mp3"},{"answer":"The idea is to bring cold water up to the surface using a submerged pipe.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/76.mp3"},{"answer":"The concept dates back to 1881...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-4-2023-01-26-23-56-17/77.mp3"}]
